    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Born to a middle-class Francophone family in Montreal in the early 1950s, Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne Dutoit was a committed Quebec sovereignist by high school and joined the F.L.Q. (Front de Lib\u00e9ration du Qu\u00e9bec), fighting in the October Crisis of 1970 &mdash; a mortal upheaval that secretly masked a @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat}-@UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.fc464242d84d4e34]{Camarilla} war. She was Embraced mid-battle by Louis de Maisonneuve of the nomadic pack the Fleur-de-Lys, and emerged its sole survivor. Disappointed that the Sabbat had no interest in an independent Quebec, she has spent decades quietly building Francophone influence, and saw her opportunity when the politically naive foreign Archbishop Valez arrived; Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne has spent a month subtly misinforming and manipulating her ever since, hoping to divide the Sabbat long enough to advance Quebec sovereignty. As a hedge, she has secretly opened contact with Annabelle, the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.jaYCq9rVOh0I9NCN]{Tremere} Camarilla prince of Quebec City.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>A dreamer and a rebel with a burning hatred of Anglophones; you refuse to speak anything but French even though fluent in English. All issues, to you, come down to language and heritage.</p><h2>Secrets</h2><p>Marie-H\u00e9l\u00e8ne has begun contacting Francophone Sabbat to identify and remove those who threaten Quebec separation. Pierre Bellemare has considered turning her to his infernal cause.</p>",
    "notes": "Embraced 1970. Apparent age: late teens. @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.paths-of-enlightenment.JournalEntry.MkHKLOcOCLQ5pWCj]{Path of Honorable Accord} 3. Disciplines (as printed): Dominate 3, Fortitude 3, Presence 4.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
